Chapter: PrimCce
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 What does each arm do with a codepoint the CCE tiers do not obviously
 cover? U+22A2 turnstile occurs once in the depot, in type-theory prose at
 Types/TypeCheckerInference.codex:8, and the zig plug's cx_cp_to_cce panics
 on it while bare metal compiles the file containing it. This asks bare metal
 what code it assigns, so the plug can match rather than invent -- the
 encoding is observable, so a made-up code diverges on every text carrying
 the character.

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni ("ascii A       " & integer-to-text (char-code-at "A" 0))
   print-line-uni ("greek Gamma   " & integer-to-text (char-code-at "Γ" 0))
   print-line-uni ("greek tau     " & integer-to-text (char-code-at "τ" 0))
   print-line-uni ("turnstile     " & integer-to-text (char-code-at "⊢" 0))
   print-line-uni ("turnstile len " & integer-to-text (text-length "⊢"))
   print-line-uni ("roundtrip     " & "⊢")
  end
